The attached image (Figure 4) illustrates the enhanced uptake of antigens by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs) when formulated with Nano-11 nanoparticles. Confocal microscopy shows that Nano-11 (red) and ovalbumin (OVA, green) are minimally taken up when presented individually. However, when OVA is adsorbed to Nano-11 (OVA+Nano-11), both are efficiently phagocytized by BMDCs and demonstrate clear co-localization within the cells. This indicates Nano-11's effectiveness as a delivery vehicle for negatively charged protein antigens, significantly enhancing antigen uptake and promoting subsequent immune activation.